    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Seismic design of reinforced concrete mat foundations has advanced significantly in the last twenty years. As\r\nanalytical capabilities have improved, primarily in the form of finite element analysis, the mathematical modeling of\r\nthese continuous structural elements has led to seemingly more precise designs. Yet, fundamental questions still remain regarding the seismic performance of these thick foundation systems.\r\n\r\nThis Technical Brief attempts to address what is known and what is unknown about this subject, so that a structural\r\nengineer can proceed with a seismic design in an informed manner. Because many of the parameters associated with a\r\nmat foundation design can be highly variable, designs that consider this variability are encouraged.\r\n\r\nThis Technical Brief is organized to lead the reader through the following sequence of topics:\r\n• What is a Mat Foundation?\r\n• Historical Perspectives\r\n• Soil Properties\r\n• Soil-Structure Interaction\r\n• Load Combinations\r\n• Proportioning\r\n• Analysis\r\n• Design\r\n• Mats Supported on Deep Foundation Elements\r\n• Detailing\r\n• Constructability Issues",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Klemencic, Ron and McFarlane, Ian S and Hawkins, Neil M and Nikolaou, Sissy. (2012). Seismic Design of Reinforced Concrete Mat Foundations. CUREE - NIST NEHRP Seismic Design Technical Brief Number 7. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at: http://purl.stanford.edu/qh977zt9377",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
            "displayLabel": "Preferred Citation",
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
